  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but consistent relationship between bleomycin and S-117, mediated through the enzyme 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid. Bleomycin is directly linked to this compound, which in turn targets S-117. This pathway is reinforced by multiple independent connections, all with high confidence scores, indicating a robust biological link. The presence of multiple targets (A388, COLO-792, and Lysine-specific demethylase 4C) further supports the idea that 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid acts as a central mediator in the interaction between bleomycin and S-117. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where bleomycin influences the activity of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which then modulates S-117. This suggests that the relationship between bleomycin and S-117 is not direct but rather indirect, through a shared biochemical pathway.",
